    [?] /memory - manage work memory (list items, forget some, edit some, etc)
        [ ] Not sure is this is really needed. The LLM should be able to manage its own memory.
        
        [ ] possibly add bangs ? !important to mark as to memorize or something. 
        !instructions to mark as system instructions, etc. This way the LLM can decide what to memorize and what not, and we can also use it to give it instructions on how to manage its memory.
            [ ] add /instruct command to instruct the LLM important infos that it should remember for the whole conversation
                -> then store into the system prompt or something like that.
            
                examples:
                    /instruct in the shell, always use `pixi run` prefix to access python environment for the project.
                    /instruct when coding assembly always use GNU assembly syntax and not intel
                    /instruct when modifying a file, always document your approach in a comment at the top of the code unit your are modifying.
            
            [ ] Support for global instructions ? 
                - kinda on the territory of custom system prompts

